# Opus Quad fixture: constructed-opus-keep-alive
# Constructed from the documented layout, not a capture: no published
# source quotes the bytes of the Opus Quad's own keep-alive. The analysis
# only says it "always starts with 51 73 70 74 31 57 6d 4a 4f 4c 06" and is
# similar to the CDJ keep-alive
#   (https://github.com/kyleawayan/opus-quad-pro-dj-link-analysis/blob/main/README.md#2-initialization),
# and beat-link recognises it as a 0x36-byte keep-alive named "OPUS-QUAD"
#   (https://github.com/Deep-Symmetry/beat-link/blob/main/src/main/java/org/deepsymmetry/beatlink/DeviceAnnouncement.java).
# Layout: https://djl-analysis.deepsymmetry.org/djl-analysis/startup.html#cdj-keep-alive
# Documented in: docs/protocols/opus-quad.md#what-the-unit-sends
# Values are invented for the test: device 0x01, MAC 02:00:00:00:00:09,
# IP 192.168.2.10, 2 peers.
# Bytes: UDP payload, hex, 16 per line.
51 73 70 74 31 57 6d 4a 4f 4c 06 00 4f 50 55 53
2d 51 55 41 44 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00
01 02 00 36 01 01 02 00 00 00 00 09 c0 a8 02 0a
02 00 00 00 01 00
